{
  "id": "lab-grades-the-pull-request-merge",
  "origin": "inventory",
  "behaviour": "The lab grades the same test merge commit GitHub Actions grades for a pull request. A pull request head event keeps the pull request number, 0 for every other event. Before it expands a pull request or hotfix grade that is not a plant, the scheduler resolves GitHub's test merge of that pull request and takes it only when the merge's second parent is the head; while GitHub has none yet, or never answers, the head is held and tried again, and after UNMERGED_TRIES such tries the lab gives up and grades the bare head against its event base, remembered on the grade as a fallback. With a resolved merge, the graded commit's tree and files feed the static unit keys and the worker's checkout, the merge's first parent is the merge base its units diff against, the grader revision stays the event's own base, and the head stays the head on every check run, lane and piece of evidence. A lease of such a grade carries the graded commit beside the head, base and grader; its worker reads github.sha as the graded commit and fetches it through a git bundle the scheduler serves when its own node mirror lacks the merge. The grade's identity includes the graded commit once resolved, so a rerequest after dev moved and a newer merge resolved grades under a new key, while a grade with no resolved merge keeps the key it always had. Merge group, push, promotion, notice and plant grades are unchanged.",
  "seam": "scripts.ci_lab.webhooks.head_events and head_data over a pull_request or rerequested check_run delivery, scripts.ci_lab.scheduler.Scheduler.tick over its fakes with a merges port that resolves, pends, or finds no merge, scripts.ci_lab.scheduler.MirrorExpander.expand and bundle over a real git repository, scripts.ci_lab.executors.static and _context over a lease naming a graded commit, scripts.ci_lab.lease_api the /bundle route, and scripts.ci_lab.digests.grade_key over GradeInputs with a graded commit",
